{% set distributor = frappe.get_doc("Distributor", doc.distributor ) %}

<article>
    <div class="logo-container">
      <div class="logo-left-margin"></div>
      <div class="logo">
          <img class="meril" src="/assets/lms/images/meril.svg" alt="Meril" />
        </div>
     </div>
  <h4>Compliance Code of Conduct for Meril Distributors</h4>
  <section>
    <h5 data-num="1">INTRODUCTION</h5> 
    <p>Meril aim is to improve the quality of human life through innovative and advanced healthcare solutions. To achieve this, we continually work towards innovation in manufacturing medical technology. Meril collaborates with physicians to identify unmet clinical needs, develop revolutionary therapies and work towards bringing new advancement in its products.  It is also important that such advancement in medical field should reach to larger group and more patients get benefit of available therapies and add More to Life. In the course of such interaction, Meril is committed to the highest standards of integrity, and adheres to the spirit of all laws and regulations of the countries in which it operates whether such business is carried out through direct sales operations or through Distributors. To enable this goal, it is important to adhere to ethical and legal standards in our interaction with Health Care Professionals/Health Care Organizations.  In view of the same, a definitive Compliance Code of Conduct by Meril Distributors have been defined and presented to the Distributor for due compliance of the same.</p>

    <p class="mt-3">Meril Companies :  <strong>{%- if distributor.meril_company_table and distributor.meril_company_table|length > 0 -%}
                    {%- for c in distributor.meril_company_table -%}
                        {{ c.meril_company_name }}{%- if not loop.last %}, {% endif -%}
                    {%- endfor -%}
                {%- else -%}
                    ______
                {%- endif -%} </strong> are hereinafter referred to as “Meril”. 
</p>
      <p> {{ distributor.distributor_company_name }} is hereinafter referred to as “Distributor”</p>
        <p>It is warranted from the Distributors to observe and adhere to this Code of Conduct.  Failure to comply may result in termination of the commercial relationship with Meril and Distributor will be responsible for any other legal implication.
</p>
    <h5 data-num="2">APPLICABILITY</h5>
    <p>This policy is applicable to any person or legal entity who is and/or proposed to be, engaged and/or working for or on behalf of Meril for sale, marketing, promotion, or distribution of Meril’s products, including but not limited to dealers, agents, resellers, distributors, business partners, consultants, contractors, marketing support, brokers or advisors who buy and resell Meril’s products and/or earn a commission on the sale of Meril’s products.</p>
    <h5 data-num="3">COMPLIANCE WITH LAWS </h5>
    <p>Meril is committed to comply with Indian laws and laws of other countries that are, or may be, of potential relevance, including but not limited to laws applicable to bribery, and/or corrupt payments, including, National Medical Commission Act (NMC), Uniform Code of Pharmaceuticals and Marketing Practices (UCPMP), Drugs and Magical Remedies Act, National Pharmaceutical Pricing Authority (NPPA), Goods and Service Tax, Income Tax, Prevention of Corruption Act (PoCA), all applicable national, regional, provincial, state, municipal or local laws and regulations that prohibit tax evasion, or otherwise dealing in the bribery of, or the providing of, facilitation payments, or other benefits to, any government official or any other person.     This Compliance Code of Conduct is applicable to all the individuals, distributors, agents, channel partners, acting on behalf of Meril.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="s2">
        <div class="logo-container">
      <div class="logo-left-margin"></div>
      <div class="logo">
          <img class="meril" src="/assets/lms/images/meril.svg" alt="Meril" />
        </div>
     </div>
    <h4>Compliance Code of Conduct for Meril Distributors</h4>
    <h5 data-num="4" >BOOKS AND RECORDS</h5>
    <p>Distributor shall keep complete, genuine, accurate and timely records of all expenses and transactions pertaining to sales and marketing of Meril products or services. All such transactions must be recorded with reasonable details along with supporting documents in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles.
</p>
    <h5 data-num="5">CONFLICTS OF INTEREST</h5>
    <p>Distributor shall avoid actual or apparent conflicts of interest and should make sound Business decisions in the best interests of Meril, undistorted by personal interests. A conflict of interest may exist whenever a Distributor’s private interests or personal Activities or relationships interfere or appear to interfere with the duties warranted towards Meril. If you discover that a personal activity, investment, interest or Association compromises – or even appear to compromise – your objectivity or ability to make impartial business decisions, disclose it immediately to your designated Meril sales representative and Business Head, who will contact the Meril Compliance Head to obtain approval, if appropriate.
</p>
    <h5 data-num="6">TRAINING AND EDUCATION OF HEALTHCARE PROVIDERS
</h5><p>Training and Education programs are important for safe and effective use of Meril products. Programs can include hands on sessions, lectures, presentations on topics related to Meril product or therapies. If there is a need for a Distributor to conduct such training and education program, a separate written communication to be made to Meril and follow the process suggested for the same. 
</p>
    <h5 data-num="7">GIFTS, TRAVELS, OR ENTERTAINMENT</h5>
    <p>Gifts, travel and entertainment offerings that give the appearance of improper business advantage are strictly prohibited. If there is a need for Distributors to extend any reasonable support , a separate written communication to be made to Meril and follow the process suggested for the same. Such gifts, travel, and entertainment should be permitted under applicable laws, modest in value, infrequent, reasonable and for a legitimate purpose.
</p>
    <h5 data-num="8">EDUCATIONAL GRANTS</h5>
    <p>Educational Grants are permitted only if the grant is intended for Scientific, Educational, Charity and better patient outcome purposes. Such Grants should be independent and not linked with the volume or value of purchases made by, or anticipated from, the grant recipients. If there is a need for Distributors to provide the same, a separate written communication to be made to Meril and follow the process suggested for the same.
</p>
  </section>
  <section class="s3">
        <div class="logo-container">
      <div class="logo-left-margin"></div>
      <div class="logo">
          <img class="meril" src="/assets/lms/images/meril.svg" alt="Meril" />
        </div>
     </div>
    <h4>Compliance Code of Conduct for Meril Distributors</h4>
    <h5 data-num="9">DISCOUNTS/REBATES & COMMISSION
</h5>
    <p>Discounts/Rebates and Commission must be defined and approved before the time of sale in form of written contract between the parties and must not result in personal benefit to any HCP/HCO or government official.
</p>
    <h5 data-num="10">COMPLIANCE WITH POLICY AND TERMINATION ON NON-COMPLIANCE
</h5>
    <p>It is the responsibility of the Distributor to ensure that their Representatives understand and comply with Meril Distributor’s Compliance Code of Conduct Policy, and the Distributor shall self-monitor their adherence to this Code of Conduct. The Distributor understand and acknowledges that if it is determined or believed that at any time a Distributor or its Representatives have failed to comply with the standards set forth in this Code of Conduct, then Meril shall have all right to determine the relationship without notice and without any liability or obligation of any nature whatsoever. </p>
    <h6>SELF – DECLARATION CERTIFICATION OF COMPLIANCE</h6>
    <p>I have read and understood Meril Distributor Compliance Code of Conduct and hereby declare that I will adhere in all respects to the ethics and standards of conducts described in it. I further confirm my understanding that any non-adherence may be subject to appropriate disciplinary action, which may include termination of the commercial relationship with Meril. This policy supplements, but does not supersede, any and all rights maintained by Meril under any contract with the Distributor.
</p>

 <div class="bottom">
 <div class="relative"><span class="sign">Sign & Seal:  _________________________</span> 
      <span class="datetime"> {{ frappe.utils.format_datetime( doc.submission_datetime, "d MMMM yyyy hh:mm a") }} [SYSTEM GENERATED]</span>
      <div class="seal">
       <div class="circle">
        <div class="text">
            {# compute how many characters we have #}
            {% set my_text = distributor.distributor_company_name + " • " %}
           {% set letters = my_text.replace(' ', ' ') | list %}
           {% set count = letters | length %}
           {% for char in letters %}
            {% set angle = (loop.index0 * 360) / count %}
            <span style="-webkit-transform: rotate({{ angle }}deg)">{{ char }}</span>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <img class="ring" src="/assets/lms/images/seal-border.png" alt="seal" />
    </div>
    </div>
 </div>
 <p>{{ distributor.attendee_name}}, {{ distributor.designation }} </p>
 <p>{{ distributor.distributor_company_name }} </p>
<p>{{distributor.distributor_contact_number}}, {{ distributor.distributor_email_address}} </p>
<p>{{ distributor.distributor_company_address }}</p>
</div>
  </section>
</article>

<style>
      *{
  font-family: sans-serif;
  font-size: 15px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  text-align: justify;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 0;
}


.seal{
    display: none;
}
.relative{
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
}
.s2{
    padding-top: 1cm;
}

.s3{
    padding-top: 2cm;
}
 .logo-container {
    width: 100%;
    display: -webkit-box;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .logo-left-margin {
    flex: 1;
    -webkit-box-flex: 1;
    height: 100px;
  }

  .logo {
    display: block;
    width: fit-content;
    margin-left: auto;
    position: relative;
  }

  .logo span {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: -0.3cm;
    transform: translate(-50%, -80%);
     -webkit-transform: translate(-50%, -80%);
    left: 50%;
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-family: sans-serif;
    color: #999;
  }

.meril{
  width: 120px;
  font-family: sans-serif;
}
.print-format{
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
}

@media screen {
   .print-format{
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 2cm;
}
}
h4{
  text-align: center;
  padding: 0.2cm;
  margin-top: 0.1cm;
  color: #fff !important;
  background: #5291cd;
}
article{
  padding: 0;
  page-break-inside: avoid;
  page-break-after: always;
}

h5{
  position: relative;
  font-weight: 500;
  margin: 0.4cm 0;
  font-size: 0.4cm;
}
h5::before{
  content: "1.";
  position: absolute;
  left: -1cm
}
h5[data-num="2"]::before{
     content: "2.";
}
h5[data-num="3"]::before{
     content: "3.";
}
h5[data-num="4"]::before{
     content: "4.";
}
h5[data-num="5"]::before{
     content: "5.";
}
h5[data-num="6"]::before{
     content: "6.";
}
h5[data-num="7"]::before{
     content: "7.";
}
h5[data-num="8"]::before{
     content: "8.";
}
h5[data-num="9"]::before{
     content: "9.";
}
h5[data-num="10"]::before{
     content: "10.";
}

h6{
    text-align: center;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 20px;
    margin-top: 2cm;
}

p{
   text-align: justify;
   z-index: 1;
   position: relative;
}

img{
  width: 4cm;
  display: block;
  margin-left: auto;
}
.bottom{
    margin-top: 2cm;
}

.datetime{
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-left: 0.3cm;
}

.seal{ position: absolute; top: -2cm; left: 1cm;  opacity: 0.8; z-index: -1;;}
.circle { position: relative; width: 130px; height: 130px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; }
    .text { position: absolute;top:62%;left: 50%;-webkit-transform: translate(-50%, -50%); width: 100%; height: 100%; }
    .text span { position: absolute; left: 50%;font-size: 1em;color: red;font-weight: 600; -webkit-transform-origin: 0 50px;     font-family:  "Courier New", monospace; }
    .ring{  width: 130px !important;height: 130px !important; }

@page {
  size: A4 portrait; /* Set page size to A4 and orientation to portrait */
  margin: 0; /* Apply a 2cm margin on all sides */
}
</style>
